; DOMAIN: probability/entropic-optimal-transport [CLOSED, derived 2026-07-26]
; Claim: The Schrodinger bridge is the entropic regularization of optimal transport and the dynamic bridge between diffusion and Monge-Kantorovich. (1) Static problem: minimize relative entropy KL(pi || R) over couplings pi with fixed marginals mu,nu, where R is the reference (Brownian/heat) kernel — equivalently entropic-OT min <c,pi> + eps H(pi). (2) Dynamic Schrodinger problem: minimize KL(P || W^eps) over path measures P with fixed endpoint marginals, W^eps = reference Brownian motion with variance eps. (3) Small-noise limit: as eps->0, eps * (optimal entropic cost) Gamma-converges to (1/2)W2^2 and the bridge converges to the displacement (McCann) geodesic. (4) Solution structure: pi*(x,y) = a(x) R(x,y) b(y) (Sinkhorn/IPF fixed point), the entropic analogue of Kantorovich potentials. (5) Large-deviations origin: the bridge is the most likely path of a cloud of independent Brownian particles conditioned on empirical endpoint marginals (Schilder/Sanov), so its rate functional IS the transport cost.
; Structure: (static: min_pi KL(pi||R) s.t. marginals mu,nu) (dynamic: min_P KL(P||W^eps) fixed endpoints) (Sinkhorn factorization pi*=a(x)R(x,y)b(y)) (eps->0: eps*cost -> (1/2)W2^2, bridge -> displacement geodesic) (LDP: bridge = conditioned Brownian cloud, rate functional = transport cost).
; Result: Optimal transport, heat diffusion, and large-deviations conditioning are unified: entropic-OT interpolates between the heat kernel (eps large) and quadratic Monge-Kantorovich (eps->0), solved by iterative Sinkhorn scaling, and its very definition is the large-deviation rate of a diffusing particle cloud pinned at its endpoints.
; Bridge: genesis_heat_kernel_varadhan (the Schrodinger reference measure IS the heat kernel, and the eps->0 collapse of entropic cost to (1/2)W2^2 is the integrated form of Varadhan's -2t log p_t -> d^2; both say vanishing-noise diffusion recovers geodesic distance) + genesis_wasserstein_gradient_flow_JKO (the small-noise limit of the dynamic bridge is exactly the W2 displacement geodesic whose gradient flow of entropy is the heat equation — Schrodinger bridges are the entropically-smoothed geodesics of Otto's W2 geometry) + genesis_large_deviations (the bridge is defined by conditioning a Brownian cloud on its empirical marginals; Schilder/Sanov give the rate functional, and KL(P||W) minimization is literally the LDP variational principle) + genesis_ricci_flow (the reference heat kernel carries curvature via Li-Yau bounds, so Ric>=K controls the entropic cost's concentration and the bridge's contraction, matching CD(K,infty) W2-contraction).